  "body": "As discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/javascript/issues/29, ECMA262 caught up with reality enough that we could obsolete the document.\n\nI think this means removing:\n\n> User agents must follow the additions and clarifications made in the WHATWG JavaScript standard. [JAVASCRIPT]\n\nas well as the line\n\n> JavaScript Standard, M. Bynens. WHATWG.\n\nfrom the references list.\n\nWe _could_ insert something like\n\n> User agents should carefully consider [the issues tagged \"web reality\"](https://github.com/tc39/ecma262/labels/web%20reality) when implementing the JavaScript specification.\n\nif we wanted. Anyone have thoughts on that?\n",
